IMPORT prelude

-- coa26-support.l4: three-valued helpers for the coa26 modules (Companies Act 2006, Part 42, ss 1209-1238).
-- They implement no provision of the Act, so their names begin with the part's own prefix `coa26 support`
-- (no other part can define such a name) instead of a section label.
--
-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING (NOTHING is "not covered", never FALSE). These are the
-- strong Kleene connectives: a JUST FALSE decides a conjunction and a JUST TRUE decides a disjunction even when
-- the other answer is NOTHING; otherwise NOTHING passes through. Nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST x THEN x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST x THEN (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`coa26 support the answer is NOTHING` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST x THEN FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support a fact as an answer` MEANS JUST b

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support the opposite answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      q IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support both answers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` p THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` q THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` p AND `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` q THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN p IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      q IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support either answer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` p THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` q THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` p AND `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` q THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support any of the answers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` answers THEN JUST TRUE
        IF all `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` answers THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`coa26 support all of the answers` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` answers THEN JUST FALSE
        IF all `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` answers THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
